course: dictionary
lesson: 3395
title: Expensive: costing a lot
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Expensive means costing a lot of money. Something expensive has a high price, so you need more money to buy it. Its opposite is cheap.
explain: «Before printing, books in Europe were copied by hand, so they were rare and very expensive.» The clues are copied by hand and rare: a book written out by hand took a very long time, so it cost a lot of money.
explain: To find out which thing is more expensive, compare the prices and subtract the smaller price from the bigger one to see how much more. Expensive changes its form too: more expensive, most expensive.
fact: Expensive means costing a lot of money.
fact: The opposite of expensive is cheap.
fact: More expensive compares two things; most expensive compares three or more.
fact: «Toad ... has ordered a large and very expensive motor-car» shows that he has plenty of money to spend.
fact: A thing can be a need or a want: plain shoes are a need, and «expensive branded trainers» are a want.
exercise: «Before printing, books were copied by hand, so they were very expensive.» What does expensive mean? | *Costing a lot of money | Written in pencil | Very old and worn | Easy to find in any shop
exercise: A bag costs £3 and another bag costs £12. How much more expensive is the £12 bag? | £3 | £12 | *£9 | £15
exercise: «Toad has ordered a large and very expensive motor-car.» What does this suggest about Toad? | He is very small | He is poor and has no money | He does not like cars | *He has a lot of money to spend
test: Which word means the opposite of expensive? | Costly | Large | Rare | *Cheap
test: Ravi's bike costs £80, Sam's bike costs £120 and Mia's bike costs £200. Which bike is the most expensive? | They all cost the same | Ravi's bike | *Mia's bike | Sam's bike
exam: Why should you ask before using a parent's card, when «games and apps can become expensive»? | Because cards are always free | *Because the costs can add up to a lot of money | Because apps cannot cost any money | Because games are always cheap
